cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "A cut and independent-set bound for sparse halves"
message: "If you refer to this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Argudo"
    given-names: "Pablo Miguel"
abstract: >-
  A partial bound of 2587/100000 for sparse halves in triangle-free graphs
  (Erdos problem 128), assuming the Balogh-Clemen-Lidicky max-cut theorem.
  Elementary: no flag algebra or semidefinite certificate. Includes two
  independent exact-arithmetic verifiers and a Lean 4 certificate for the
  scalar optimization. Not a solution of the problem; no priority claimed.
keywords:
  - extremal graph theory
  - triangle-free graphs
  - sparse halves
  - Erdos problem 128
license: CC-BY-4.0
date-released: "2026-09-09"
